@startuml
title Editing a diagram
start
:Type PlantUML or Mermaid;
:The language is detected from the text and the file name;
:Findings are underlined while you type;
:A state diagram is checked as a state machine,
and a sequence diagram against the state machines
of its folder;
:F5 plays it: 1–9 take a step, Space the next,
← back, Esc stops;
:Play a recorded trace (in the command menu) plays
a log of the machine (JSON Lines, *.jsonl) line by line;
if (a block hides the lines you want?) then (fold it)
  :Ctrl+Shift+[ folds the block at the caret;
  :Ctrl+Shift+] unfolds it;
else (leave it open)
  :Keep the source in view;
endif
:Ctrl+Shift+I formats the diagram;
:A click on an error in the status bar jumps to its line;
:Ctrl+click on a label or a line in the diagram jumps there too;
:Alt and a drag on a line in the diagram moves that part of it,
and a double click with Alt gives it back to the layout;
stop
@enduml
